What is HTTP?
    
    Hyper Text Transfer Protocol and connects clients to servers.
    
What is a URL?
    
    Uniform Resource Locator and is a resource address online.
    
What is DNS?
    
    Domain Name System and converts URL into IP addresses.
    
What is a query string?
    
    It allows you to pass key-value pairs into the URL, in the format `?key1=value1&key2=value2...` (updated to add format example from verifying on the solution page) 
    
List two HTTP Verbs and their use cases.
    
    GET (gathers "some" data from the server) and POST (sends "some" data to the server)

What is an HTTP request?
    
    A request from a client to a server following HTTP protocol
    
What is an HTTP response?
    
    A response from a server to a client following HTTP protocol
    
What is an HTTP header? Give a couple examples of request and response headers you have seen. (Had to use the solution page to verify I used the right examples and added all listed. I had only cookies and cache examples)
    
    Headers provide additional information about the request/response. Request headers: Host, User-Agent, Accept, Cookie, Cache-Control; Response headers: Content-Type, Last-Modified, Set-Cookie, Cache-Control

What happens when you type a URL in a browser?
    The browser reates an IP address from DNS and makes a request to that IP address. Server sends a response and browser makes a DOM and then creates separate requests for other resources and receives responses from each
